# Build tags selecting the gotreesitter grammar subset embedded in the satellites
# CLI (the `code index` symbol extractor — epic:code-index, sty_380a116d).
#
# Single source of truth, consumed by BOTH the Makefile and the release workflow
# so the local and shipped binaries embed the same languages. `grammar_subset`
# turns on selective embedding; each `grammar_subset_<lang>` adds one grammar.
# Adding a language = add its tag here (no other file changes). Languages NOT
# listed are simply unrecognised by `code index` (they degrade to "no symbols",
# never a crash). The full 206-grammar set is the default build (no tags) and
# costs ~+28 MB; this curated set keeps the binary small.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments; the build joins the rest into one -tags arg.
grammar_subset
grammar_subset_go
grammar_subset_python
grammar_subset_javascript
grammar_subset_typescript
grammar_subset_tsx
grammar_subset_rust
grammar_subset_java
grammar_subset_ruby
grammar_subset_c
grammar_subset_cpp
grammar_subset_c_sharp
grammar_subset_php
grammar_subset_bash
